## [Unreleased]

Work completed since the 1.0.0 entry below was drafted.
**v1.0.0 has not been tagged yet** — RC1 is pending the soak
test described in `PROJECT_TRACKER.md`.

### Fixed

- **Print window input freeze** — printing via a popup window
  could leave the entire application unresponsive to mouse and
  keyboard until the tab was manually refreshed. Root cause: a
  documented Chrome bug where a popup used for printing can
  fail to hand OS-level input focus back to its opener.
  `openPrintWindow()` now prints from a hidden `<iframe>`
  instead of `window.open()`, which has no second window for
  focus to get lost between.
- **Duplicate rooms could still be printed.** Save correctly
  blocked a group with a duplicate room, but `printRegister()`
  and `printRoomingList()` read the live register directly with
  no validation at all. Both now run the same check Save uses
  before printing anything.
- **Duplicate-room detection was asymmetric.** Only the second
  occurrence of a repeated room was ever flagged — the first
  looked completely valid. Both the save-blocking check and the
  on-screen red-cell check now flag every row involved.
- Validation messages referenced "Row N"; changed to "Sr N" to
  match the visible column header exactly.
- All remaining native `alert()`/`prompt()` calls in
  `printing.js` (including one in `printBlankRegister()` that
  had been missed in the original dialog-system conversion)
  replaced with the app's own dialog system.
- A manifest print for a date with zero scheduled groups now
  prints a usable 25-row blank register with a note explaining
  why, instead of a bare "no data" message.
- Arrival Date no longer accepts a date before today, at the
  calendar-picker level and as a backstop on manual entry.
- Bulk apply of one meal plan to every row in the register.
- Removed a harmless duplicate call to
  `initializeReportPrinting()` in the application bootstrap.

### Added

- **Multiple guests per room.** Guest Name now accepts more
  than one line, added via a real button or the Down Arrow key,
  capped by the room's occupancy limit from Room Master. New
  lines always append at the true end of the text regardless of
  cursor position, so guests can never be inserted out of order.
- **Departure dates — data model.** Groups now carry a default
  departure date and night count; individual rooms can override
  it. Every room tracks its own checkout state independently.
  Existing saved groups are migrated automatically. This is the
  foundation for the in-progress departure-date feature — see
  `CLAUDE.md` §14 for the full specification and
  `PROJECT_TRACKER.md` §5 for live phase status.

### Changed

- `css/style.css` fully deduplicated and reorganized into 22
  named sections. 43 duplicated selectors resolved (several
  from whole sections having been pasted in twice across the
  development session); 3 dead pseudo-element rules removed.

