## [1.0.0] — 2026-07-30

First release. Front office software for hotel group arrivals.

### Added — Arrival Register

- Group header: name, arrival date, agent, prepared by,
  status, collapsible notes
- Row generation by count, single row add, room sorting
- **Auto Room Series** — assigns rooms from the Room Master,
  walking real inventory rather than counting upward, so gaps
  are skipped instead of invented
- Live **room category** column, filled as a room number is typed
- **Pax auto-fill** from the room's category default
- **Children** count with an age field per child (0–17)
- Meal plan per room — EP, CP, MAP, AP
- VIP flag and special request per room
- Input rules: room 3 digits, pax 2 digits, guest name 60
  characters, mobile 15 characters, special request 80
- **Enter** moves down the same column
- Register search across room, guest, mobile and request
- Sticky column headers and a sticky totals bar
- Live summary: rooms, pax, EP/CP/MAP/AP

### Added — Room Master

- Room categories with rename and delete
- Room inventory by single room, range or mixed list
- Bulk setup from pasted text
- **Occupancy rules per category** — default adults, max
  adults, max children, max occupancy
- Inventory summary with bed capacity
- Search across room number and category
- **Manager PIN** protecting the page from accidental changes

### Added — Occupancy control

- **Max Occupancy caps the total people in a room.** Children
  are a subset of pax, never an addition, so moving a person
  from the adult column to the child column cannot create
  space. The loophole is structurally impossible rather than
  policed.
- Children field hard-capped live to
  `min(maxChildren, pax)`
- Save **blocked**, not warned, on rooms outside the Room
  Master, duplicate rooms within a group, or any capacity breach
- Red cell and reason shown in the Category column

### Added — Rooming List

- Automatic view of the open group
- Category, VIP and special request columns
- Sort by room
- Blank rows excluded
- CSV export

### Added — Dashboard

- KPI cards: groups, rooms, guests, today's arrivals
- Arrival Control Center: status counts, VIP guests, meal
  covers, allocated rooms
- Today's and tomorrow's arrival cards, click to open
- Saved Groups with search, status badges and last-modified

### Added — Reports

On screen, with **Current Group** and **All Groups** scopes:

- Arrival summary, meal summary, occupancy summary, room
  category
- Filters in All Groups mode: arrival date range, status, agent
- Live count of how many groups a filter matches
- **Occupancy reported per arrival date**, because a room reused
  on different dates cannot be summed into a single percentage
- **Cross-group double-booking detection** — same room, same
  date, two groups
- Warning when guests have no meal plan set

### Added — Printable reports

- **Daily Arrival Manifest** — front office and duty manager
- **Housekeeping Allocation Sheet** — grouped by category with
  subtotals
- **Food & Beverage Covers Sheet** — including breakfast, lunch
  and dinner counts derived from meal plans
- **Management Flash** — date range, occupancy per date, business
  by agent, attention list

### Added — Printing

- Central print engine, A4 landscape, repeating column headers,
  no rows split across pages
- Group Arrival Register with signature column and sign-off block
- Blank register with tall handwriting rows
- Rooming list for Housekeeping
- Document headers carrying hotel, group, date, agent, prepared
  by and print timestamp
- Room categories never printed

### Added — Data and safety

- **One-step restore** — Clear Register, Generate Rows and Bulk
  Import snapshot the register first and offer to restore
- **Unsaved draft recovery** with a Keep / Discard banner,
  schema-versioned so a draft from an older layout is discarded
  rather than loaded
- Autosave within a second of any edit, plus a 15-second backstop
- Save confirmation toast on every write
- Database backup and restore as JSON
- **ISO 8601 timestamps** throughout
- Schema version with a migration hook
- Bulk import from pasted text
- Group JSON export and import, carrying schema version

### Added — Interface

- In-page dialogs replacing every browser `alert`, `confirm`
  and `prompt`, with red confirmation for destructive actions
- Keyboard shortcuts with an in-app reference (F1)
- Hotel name, logo and footer branding
- Collapsible notes and bulk import panels
- Register rules toggles applied immediately

### Added — Support and maintenance

- **System Diagnostics** — verifies at startup that every
  cross-module function exists, every required element is
  present, register columns match the code, no module is loaded
  twice, and reports storage usage
- Storage warning at 75%, error at 90%
- On-screen diagnostics report designed to be read out on a
  support call

### Architecture

- Nine focused JavaScript modules extracted from a single
  3,500-line file. `app.js` reduced by 80% to bootstrap and
  shared services.
- Repository pattern isolating all storage access, so moving to
  a database or API changes one file
- Controller layer — UI never refreshes modules individually
- `REGISTER_COLUMNS` as the single source of truth for every
  table cell index
- Print engine as the only route to printed output

### Fixed during development

| Issue | Effect |
|---|---|
| `saveDB()` undefined in the repository | every saved group was lost on reload |
| Saved Groups passing a filtered index to delete | searching then deleting removed the wrong group, permanently |
| `toISOString()` used for local dates | arrivals showed the wrong day before 05:30 IST — during night audit |
| `toLocaleString()` timestamps | saved groups sorted by day-of-month instead of chronologically |
| `getRegisterRows()` declared twice with different field names | blank guest names on printed registers, blank CSV exports |
| Register header row one column short of the body | every value displayed under the wrong heading |
| Five competing startup blocks | duplicate event bindings and repeated dashboard refreshes |
| `printBlankRegister()` duplicated | the wrong version ran, losing the print layout |
| `addVIPColumn()` appending headers to a table that already had them | two permanently empty columns on the Rooming List |
| `clearRegisterFields()` called but never declared | Clear Register and Discard Draft did nothing |
| Nested scrollbar in the register | two scrollbars on long groups |
| Superseded input filters left in place with old column indexes | would have silently broken the room-mode toggle |

### Known limits

- Single machine, single user
- No departure dates, so occupancy is measured on the arrival
  date only
- No rates, so no revenue, ADR or RevPAR
- Manager PIN is an accident guard, not security
- One row is one room; additional guests go in the guest name
  field as free text

